From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Reinsmidt <735251+ericreinsmidt@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] The AXP2202's first battery check after boot takes the battery
 as found instead of resetting the fuel gauge: its state started at "no
 battery", so the first check always saw one put in and reset the gauge,
 which wiped the battery model the probe had just loaded and the mark that
 says it's loaded. Every boot then loaded the model again (85 ms of I2C,
 racing the SD card's power rails on the same bus) and the gauge lost what
 it had learned. Later checks still reset it when the battery comes or goes;
 the time since a change is kept between checks, where it was an
 uninitialized local

---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/axp2202_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/axp2202_charger.c
@@ -1286,9 +1286,11 @@
 	int ret;
 	static int cnt;
 	static int rst[3] = { 1, 1, 1 };
+	static bool checked;
+	static ktime_t s_chg;
+	bool present;
 	unsigned int data;
 	uint8_t d[2];
-	ktime_t s_chg;
 	struct axp2202_device_info *di =
 		container_of(work, typeof(*di), bat_chk.work);
 
@@ -1317,7 +1319,23 @@
 	rst[cnt] = (((d[0] & GENMASK(5, 0)) << 0x08) | (d[1]));
 	if (rst[cnt] < AXP2202_VBAT_MIN)
 		rst[cnt] = 0;
+	present = rst[cnt] != 0;
 	cnt = ++cnt == 3 ? 0 : cnt;
+
+	/* The first check after the probe takes the battery as it finds it. A
+	 * battery there at boot is not one just put in, and resetting the gauge
+	 * for it, on every boot, wiped the battery model the probe had loaded,
+	 * the mark that says it's loaded (so every boot loaded it again, 85 ms
+	 * of I2C on the Brick) and what the gauge had learned. Later checks
+	 * still reset it when the battery comes or goes */
+	if (!checked) {
+		checked = true;
+		di->stat.bat_stat = present;
+		regmap_update_bits(di->regmap, AXP2202_MODULE_EN, BIT(2),
+				   present ? BIT(2) : 0);
+		WRITE_ONCE(di->stat.bat_read, present);
+		goto err_read;
+	}
 
 	/* there's one zero to indicate battery disconnect */
 	if (!rst[0] || !rst[1] || !rst[2]) {
